<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Hydaspes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">326 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-alexander-the-great">Wars of Alexander the Great</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Hydaspes was fought in 326 BCE on the banks of the Hydaspes (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhelum">Jhelum</a>) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and the Indian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porus">Porus</a>. Alexander crossed the swollen river upstream of Porus' army under cover of a storm and defeated it despite its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>. Impressed by Porus, he restored him as ruler, but his exhausted troops soon refused to march further east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-hydaspes.jpg" alt="Battle of the Hydaspes" width="320" height="138" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Fontebasso · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_the_Great_(356-23_BC)_and_Porus_(oil_on_canvas).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
